window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["gcp-ml"]=[{"id":"gcp-ml-f0001","card":"q-gcp-ml-001-1-setup-prerequisites-and-cost-control","sec":"gcp-ml-s002","q":"What does Vertex AI cover?","a":"<p>LLM integration, custom model development/tuning/deployment, notebooks, APIs, Google AI Studio for quick prototyping, and end-to-end MLOps.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0002","card":"q-gcp-ml-001-1-setup-prerequisites-and-cost-control","sec":"gcp-ml-s002","q":"What are the prerequisites for the Vertex AI course?","a":"<p>ML basics, Python ML libraries, Jupyter notebooks, and GCP core services (buckets, VMs, IAM/permissions).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0003","card":"q-gcp-ml-001-1-setup-prerequisites-and-cost-control","sec":"gcp-ml-s002","q":"What are the cost rules when learning Vertex AI (and for real work)?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Use a <strong>dedicated project</strong> and delete it when done (simplest cost control).</li>\n  <li>Set a <strong>billing alert/budget</strong>.</li>\n  <li>Use only what you need. GPUs/TPUs are costly.</li>\n  <li><strong>Stop services</strong> when idle. VMs and notebooks bill while running.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0004","card":"q-gcp-ml-001-1-setup-prerequisites-and-cost-control","sec":"gcp-ml-s002","q":"Which gcloud commands verify the CLI is installed and authenticated, and set the project?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud --version\ngcloud auth login\ngcloud config set project &lt;your-project-id&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0005","card":"q-gcp-ml-001-1-setup-prerequisites-and-cost-control","sec":"gcp-ml-s002","q":"Which commands create a dedicated learning project and link a billing account?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud projects create ml-learning-project --name=&quot;ML Learning&quot;\ngcloud config set project ml-learning-project\ngcloud billing accounts list\ngcloud billing projects link ml-learning-project --billing-account=&lt;billing-account-id&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0006","card":"q-gcp-ml-001-1-setup-prerequisites-and-cost-control","sec":"gcp-ml-s002","q":"Which gcloud command creates a $50 budget alert with thresholds at 80% and 100%?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud billing budgets create \\\n  --billing-account=&lt;billing-account-id&gt; \\\n  --display-name=&quot;Learning Budget&quot; \\\n  --budget-amount=50 \\\n  --threshold-rule=percent=0.8 \\\n  --threshold-rule=percent=1.0</code></pre></div>\n<p>In the Console: Billing, Budgets &amp; Alerts, Create Budget.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0007","card":"q-gcp-ml-001-1-setup-prerequisites-and-cost-control","sec":"gcp-ml-s002","q":"How do you stop a Vertex AI notebook instance and delete the learning project when finished?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud notebooks instances stop &lt;notebook-name&gt; --location=us-central1-a\ngcloud projects delete ml-learning-project</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0008","card":"q-gcp-ml-001-1-setup-prerequisites-and-cost-control","sec":"gcp-ml-s002","q":"What is the variant of the cost-control flow at the end of the Vertex AI course?","a":"<p>The same flow with project <code>ml-continued-learning</code>, budget 100 and thresholds 0.5/0.8/1.0, plus enabling several APIs in one command: <code>gcloud services enable aiplatform.googleapis.com notebooks.googleapis.com bigquery.googleapis.com</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0009","card":"q-gcp-ml-002-2-vertex-ai-services-map","sec":"gcp-ml-s003","q":"What are the main Vertex AI services and their use cases?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Use Case</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Vertex AI Studio</strong></td><td>Prompt design and testing of generative models</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Vertex AI Notebooks</strong></td><td>Custom model building (preferred method)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Vertex AI Pipelines</strong></td><td>MLOps: orchestrate ML workflows</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Model Registry</strong></td><td>Store and manage trained models</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Endpoints</strong></td><td>Deploy models for serving predictions</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Feature Store</strong></td><td>Manage and serve ML features</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Training</strong></td><td>Scalable custom and distributed training</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0010","card":"q-gcp-ml-002-2-vertex-ai-services-map","sec":"gcp-ml-s003","q":"What are the low-code / no-code alternatives to Vertex AI notebooks, and who are they for?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Approach</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>BigQuery ML</strong></td><td>Build models by writing SQL</td><td>Analysts who know SQL, structured data</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Vertex AI AutoML</strong></td><td>No code, bring labeled data</td><td>Teams without ML expertise</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0011","card":"q-gcp-ml-002-2-vertex-ai-services-map","sec":"gcp-ml-s003","q":"Which commands enable the APIs needed for Vertex AI?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud services enable aiplatform.googleapis.com\ngcloud services enable notebooks.googleapis.com\ngcloud services enable bigquery.googleapis.com</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0012","card":"q-gcp-ml-002-2-vertex-ai-services-map","sec":"gcp-ml-s003","q":"How do you check which models, endpoints and training jobs exist in a Vertex AI project with the Python SDK?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from google.cloud import aiplatform\naiplatform.init(project=&quot;&lt;your-project-id&gt;&quot;, location=&quot;us-central1&quot;)\nmodels = aiplatform.Model.list()\nprint(f&quot;Models in project: {len(models)}&quot;)\nendpoints = aiplatform.Endpoint.list()\nprint(f&quot;Endpoints: {len(endpoints)}&quot;)\njobs = aiplatform.CustomJob.list()\nprint(f&quot;Training jobs: {len(jobs)}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0013","card":"q-gcp-ml-003-model-garden","sec":"gcp-ml-s004","q":"What is Vertex AI Model Garden?","a":"<p>A searchable catalog of ML models and the starting point for AI applications. You can filter by modality, task, or features.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0014","card":"q-gcp-ml-003-model-garden","sec":"gcp-ml-s004","q":"What are the three types of models in Model Garden?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Foundation Models</strong></td><td>Google generative models (Gemini Pro etc.), integrated with Vertex AI Studio</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Fine-Tunable Models</strong></td><td>Customizable with your data (e.g., Meta Llama 2)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Task-Specific Solutions</strong></td><td>Pre-built for one task (object detection, syntax analysis)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0015","card":"q-gcp-ml-003-model-garden","sec":"gcp-ml-s004","q":"How do you use a Google model vs a non-Google model (like Llama 2) from Model Garden?","a":"<p>Google models open directly in Vertex AI Studio (Language Studio). Non-Google models (e.g., Llama 2) are deployed to an endpoint or opened in a Colab Enterprise notebook.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0016","card":"q-gcp-ml-003-model-garden","sec":"gcp-ml-s004","q":"How do you initialize the Vertex AI SDK and list models?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from google.cloud import aiplatform\naiplatform.init(project=&quot;&lt;your-project-id&gt;&quot;, location=&quot;us-central1&quot;)\nmodels = aiplatform.Model.list()\nfor model in models:\n    print(f&quot;{model.display_name} — {model.resource_name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0017","card":"q-gcp-ml-003-model-garden","sec":"gcp-ml-s004","q":"Which gcloud command lists Vertex AI models in a region?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud ai models list --region=us-central1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0018","card":"q-gcp-ml-004-generative-ai-models","sec":"gcp-ml-s005","q":"What do generative AI models do and which tasks do they cover?","a":"<p>They produce output from your input. Tasks: summarization, Q&amp;A, classification/sentiment, entity extraction, and content creation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0019","card":"q-gcp-ml-004-generative-ai-models","sec":"gcp-ml-s005","q":"Why does a generative model return different responses to the same prompt?","a":"<p>Its output is <strong>non-deterministic</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0020","card":"q-gcp-ml-004-generative-ai-models","sec":"gcp-ml-s005","q":"How do you generate text with Gemini Pro in the Vertex AI SDK?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import vertexai\nfrom vertexai.generative_models import GenerativeModel\nvertexai.init(project=&quot;&lt;your-project-id&gt;&quot;, location=&quot;us-central1&quot;)\nmodel = GenerativeModel(&quot;gemini-pro&quot;)\nresponse = model.generate_content(&quot;Generate a good name for a flower shop&quot;)\nprint(response.text)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0021","card":"q-gcp-ml-005-prompt-design-in-vertex-ai-studio","sec":"gcp-ml-s006","q":"How do you reach Vertex AI Studio prompt design from Model Garden?","a":"<p>Model Garden, then a Google model, then Language Studio.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0022","card":"q-gcp-ml-005-prompt-design-in-vertex-ai-studio","sec":"gcp-ml-s006","q":"Freeform vs Structured prompt mode in Vertex AI Studio?","a":"<p><strong>Freeform</strong> is an open-ended prompt. <strong>Structured</strong> is context plus input/output example pairs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0023","card":"q-gcp-ml-005-prompt-design-in-vertex-ai-studio","sec":"gcp-ml-s006","q":"What are the Vertex AI Studio sections Getting Started, My Prompts and Tune and Distill?","a":"<p><strong>Getting Started</strong> has examples. <strong>My Prompts</strong> has saved prompts (per region). <strong>Tune and Distill</strong> fine-tunes with your data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0024","card":"q-gcp-ml-005-prompt-design-in-vertex-ai-studio","sec":"gcp-ml-s006","q":"What prompt tips does Vertex AI Studio training give?","a":"<p>Be consistent in wording (always \"sentiment\", not sometimes \"answer\"). Follow Google's prompt guidance. Rate responses (improves the model). Ask for markdown output for structure. Voice input speeds iteration.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0025","card":"q-gcp-ml-005-prompt-design-in-vertex-ai-studio","sec":"gcp-ml-s006","q":"What does a freeform sentiment classification prompt look like in Vertex AI?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt = &quot;&quot;&quot;Classify the sentiment of the following tweet as positive, negative, or neutral.\nTweet: &quot;I love the new features in this update! Great work team!&quot;\nSentiment:&quot;&quot;&quot;\nresponse = model.generate_content(prompt)\nprint(response.text)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0026","card":"q-gcp-ml-005-prompt-design-in-vertex-ai-studio","sec":"gcp-ml-s006","q":"What does a structured extraction prompt with context look like in Vertex AI?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt = &quot;&quot;&quot;Answer the question using only the context provided.\nContext: The Last Glacial Maximum (LGM) was approximately 20,000 years ago,\nwhen ice sheets were at their greatest extent. Global sea levels were about\n120 meters lower than today.\nQuestion: What does LGM stand for?\nAnswer:&quot;&quot;&quot;\nresponse = model.generate_content(prompt)\nprint(response.text)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0027","card":"q-gcp-ml-005-prompt-design-in-vertex-ai-studio","sec":"gcp-ml-s006","q":"How do you control generation (temperature and output length) in the Vertex AI Gemini API?","a":"<p>Pass a <code>GenerationConfig</code> as <code>generation_config</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from vertexai.generative_models import GenerativeModel, GenerationConfig\nmodel = GenerativeModel(&quot;gemini-pro&quot;)\nconfig = GenerationConfig(temperature=0.2, max_output_tokens=256)\nresponse = model.generate_content(\n    &quot;Summarize the key benefits of cloud computing in 3 bullet points&quot;,\n    generation_config=config\n)\nprint(response.text)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0028","card":"q-gcp-ml-006-colab-enterprise","sec":"gcp-ml-s007","q":"What is Colab Enterprise?","a":"<p>A notebook environment <strong>inside your GCP project</strong>, unlike the free/pro Colab SaaS.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0029","card":"q-gcp-ml-006-colab-enterprise","sec":"gcp-ml-s007","q":"Colab (SaaS) vs Colab Enterprise?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Colab (SaaS)</th><th>Colab Enterprise</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Hosting</td><td>Google-hosted, free/pro</td><td>Within your GCP project</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Data access</td><td>Uploaded data only</td><td>Your project's data</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Use case</td><td>Quick experiments</td><td>Production-ready development</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0030","card":"q-gcp-ml-006-colab-enterprise","sec":"gcp-ml-s007","q":"Which gcloud commands create and list Colab Enterprise runtimes and templates?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud colab-enterprise runtimes create \\\n  --display-name=&quot;ml-runtime&quot; \\\n  --region=us-central1\ngcloud colab-enterprise runtimes list --region=us-central1\ngcloud colab-enterprise runtime-templates list --region=us-central1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0031","card":"q-gcp-ml-006-colab-enterprise","sec":"gcp-ml-s007","q":"What is the typical Colab Enterprise notebook setup for Gemini?","a":"<p><code>!pip install google-cloud-aiplatform</code>, then <code>vertexai.init(...)</code>, then <code>GenerativeModel(\"gemini-pro\")</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0032","card":"q-gcp-ml-007-gemini-pro-vision-multimodal","sec":"gcp-ml-s008","q":"What are the input and output of Gemini Pro Vision?","a":"<p>Input: text + image(s) or text + video. Output: text.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0033","card":"q-gcp-ml-007-gemini-pro-vision-multimodal","sec":"gcp-ml-s008","q":"What prompting strategies are recommended for Gemini Pro Vision?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Prompting strategy</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Few-shot learning</strong></td><td>Give several input examples to improve output</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Be specific</strong></td><td>Clear, detailed instructions</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Add examples</strong></td><td>Show what you expect</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Step-by-step</strong></td><td>Break complex tasks down</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Specify output format</strong></td><td>Say how to format the answer</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Image first</strong></td><td>For a single-image prompt, put the image before the text</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0034","card":"q-gcp-ml-007-gemini-pro-vision-multimodal","sec":"gcp-ml-s008","q":"Where should the image go in a single-image Gemini Pro Vision prompt?","a":"<p>Before the text (<strong>image first</strong>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0035","card":"q-gcp-ml-007-gemini-pro-vision-multimodal","sec":"gcp-ml-s008","q":"What limits and billing apply to LLM APIs?","a":"<p>All LLMs have <strong>token limits</strong> and API usage is billed <strong>per token</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0036","card":"q-gcp-ml-007-gemini-pro-vision-multimodal","sec":"gcp-ml-s008","q":"How do you extract text from an image with Gemini Pro Vision?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model = GenerativeModel(&quot;gemini-pro-vision&quot;)\nimage = Part.from_uri(&quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/image.jpg&quot;, mime_type=&quot;image/jpeg&quot;)\nresponse = model.generate_content([&quot;Read the text in this image.&quot;, image])\nprint(response.text)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0037","card":"q-gcp-ml-007-gemini-pro-vision-multimodal","sec":"gcp-ml-s008","q":"How do you do few-shot image classification with Gemini Pro Vision?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt = &quot;&quot;&quot;Look at this image and classify the animal.\nExamples:\n- A photo of a golden retriever → Dog\n- A photo of a tabby → Cat\nNow classify this image:&quot;&quot;&quot;\nimage = Part.from_uri(&quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/pet.jpg&quot;, mime_type=&quot;image/jpeg&quot;)\nresponse = model.generate_content([prompt, image])\nprint(response.text)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0038","card":"q-gcp-ml-007-gemini-pro-vision-multimodal","sec":"gcp-ml-s008","q":"How do you send a video to Gemini Pro Vision?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>video = Part.from_uri(&quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/clip.mp4&quot;, mime_type=&quot;video/mp4&quot;)\nresponse = model.generate_content([&quot;Summarize what happens in this video.&quot;, video])\nprint(response.text)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0039","card":"q-gcp-ml-008-imagen-image-model","sec":"gcp-ml-s009","q":"Where is Imagen in Model Garden and how does it relate to Gemini?","a":"<p>It is separate from Gemini and is in Model Garden under Generation, then Vision.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0040","card":"q-gcp-ml-008-imagen-image-model","sec":"gcp-ml-s009","q":"Which Imagen features were available at the time of recording?","a":"<p><strong>Caption</strong> and <strong>visual Q&amp;A</strong> were available. <strong>Image generation and mask-free editing were not publicly available.</strong></p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0041","card":"q-gcp-ml-008-imagen-image-model","sec":"gcp-ml-s009","q":"Which settings does Imagen offer?","a":"<p>Number of answers, language, and region (for regulatory needs).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0042","card":"q-gcp-ml-008-imagen-image-model","sec":"gcp-ml-s009","q":"How do you caption an image with Imagen?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from vertexai.vision_models import ImageTextModel, Image\nmodel = ImageTextModel.from_pretrained(&quot;imagetext&quot;)\nimage = Image.load_from_file(&quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/fish.jpg&quot;)\ncaptions = model.get_captions(image=image, number_of_results=1, language=&quot;en&quot;)\nprint(captions)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0043","card":"q-gcp-ml-008-imagen-image-model","sec":"gcp-ml-s009","q":"How do you ask a question about an image with Imagen?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>answers = model.ask_question(\n    image=image,\n    question=&quot;What is in this image?&quot;,\n    number_of_results=1\n)\nprint(answers)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0044","card":"q-gcp-ml-009-speech","sec":"gcp-ml-s010","q":"Which models do Speech-to-Text and Text-to-Speech use on Vertex AI?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Model</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Speech-to-Text</strong></td><td>Chirp</td><td>Audio to text</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Text-to-Speech</strong></td><td>Universal Speech Model</td><td>Synthesize speech</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0045","card":"q-gcp-ml-009-speech","sec":"gcp-ml-s010","q":"What is the limit for quick speech testing in Vertex AI Studio and what do you use for longer audio?","a":"<p>Studio testing is limited to audio of <strong>60 seconds or 10 MB</strong>. For longer audio use <strong>Speech Studio</strong> (a separate product).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0046","card":"q-gcp-ml-009-speech","sec":"gcp-ml-s010","q":"How do you synthesize speech to an MP3 file with the Text-to-Speech client?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from google.cloud import texttospeech\nclient = texttospeech.TextToSpeechClient()\ninput_text = texttospeech.SynthesisInput(text=&quot;Hello, welcome to Vertex AI.&quot;)\nvoice = texttospeech.VoiceSelectionParams(\n    language_code=&quot;en-US&quot;,\n    ssml_gender=texttospeech.SsmlVoiceGender.NEUTRAL\n)\naudio_config = texttospeech.AudioConfig(\n    audio_encoding=texttospeech.AudioEncoding.MP3\n)\nresponse = client.synthesize_speech(\n    input=input_text, voice=voice, audio_config=audio_config\n)\nwith open(&quot;output.mp3&quot;, &quot;wb&quot;) as out:\n    out.write(response.audio_content)\nprint(&quot;Audio saved to output.mp3&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0047","card":"q-gcp-ml-009-speech","sec":"gcp-ml-s010","q":"How do you transcribe a WAV file with Chirp using the Speech-to-Text client?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from google.cloud import speech\nclient = speech.SpeechClient()\nwith open(&quot;recording.wav&quot;, &quot;rb&quot;) as audio_file:\n    content = audio_file.read()\naudio = speech.RecognitionAudio(content=content)\nconfig = speech.RecognitionConfig(\n    encoding=speech.RecognitionConfig.AudioEncoding.LINEAR16,\n    language_code=&quot;en-US&quot;,\n    model=&quot;chirp&quot;\n)\nresponse = client.recognize(config=config, audio=audio)\nfor result in response.results:\n    print(f&quot;Transcript: {result.alternatives[0].transcript}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0048","card":"q-gcp-ml-010-5-get-code-and-the-studio-to-notebook-wo","sec":"gcp-ml-s011","q":"What does Get Code do in Vertex AI Studio?","a":"<p>It exports a prompt designed in Studio as Python, Node.js, Java, curl, or <strong>Open in Colab Enterprise</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0049","card":"q-gcp-ml-010-5-get-code-and-the-studio-to-notebook-wo","sec":"gcp-ml-s011","q":"How do you call the Gemini Pro API with curl?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>curl -X POST \\\n  -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth print-access-token)&quot; \\\n  -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; \\\n  &quot;https://us-central1-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/projects/&lt;your-project-id&gt;/locations/us-central1/publishers/google/models/gemini-pro:generateContent&quot; \\\n  -d &#x27;{\n    &quot;contents&quot;: [{&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;parts&quot;: [{&quot;text&quot;: &quot;What does LGM stand for?&quot;}]}]\n  }&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0050","card":"q-gcp-ml-010-5-get-code-and-the-studio-to-notebook-wo","sec":"gcp-ml-s011","q":"What is the solution flow of the challenge to select and test a GenAI model in Vertex AI?","a":"<ol>\n  <li>Model Garden, filter Generation, Language, pick <strong>Gemini Pro</strong> (newest, integrated in Studio; skip PaLM 2/text-bison as older, Codey as code-specific).</li>\n  <li>View Details, Open Language Studio, paste the email prompt, iterate, <strong>save</strong> it.</li>\n  <li><strong>Get Code</strong>, Python with the model settings, <strong>Open Notebook</strong> (Colab Enterprise), authenticate, pip install, run.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0051","card":"q-gcp-ml-010-5-get-code-and-the-studio-to-notebook-wo","sec":"gcp-ml-s011","q":"Which generation settings does the Get Code challenge use?","a":"<p><code>max_output_tokens=1024, temperature=0.9, top_p=1.0</code> and an email-writing prompt.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0052","card":"q-gcp-ml-010-5-get-code-and-the-studio-to-notebook-wo","sec":"gcp-ml-s011","q":"What roles do Model Garden, Vertex AI Studio, Get Code and Colab Enterprise play in rapid prototyping?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Model Garden</strong></td><td>Discover and select models</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Vertex AI Studio</strong></td><td>Design, test, save prompts</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Get Code</strong></td><td>Export prompt as code</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Colab Enterprise</strong></td><td>Notebook to build applications on the API</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0053","card":"q-gcp-ml-011-6-tensorflow-and-mnist-on-vertex-ai","sec":"gcp-ml-s012","q":"What is TensorFlow and why prefer it on GCP?","a":"<p>An open-source library from Google Brain (used by Google, Airbnb, Uber, Netflix) for image recognition, NLP, speech and predictive modeling. On GCP it integrates deeply with Vertex AI, so prefer it for custom models where possible.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0054","card":"q-gcp-ml-011-6-tensorflow-and-mnist-on-vertex-ai","sec":"gcp-ml-s012","q":"How does TensorFlow integrate with Vertex AI?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Integration</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Pre-installed in Notebooks</td><td>Ready in notebook instances</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Custom Training</td><td>Submit TF jobs to Vertex AI Training</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Pre-built Containers</td><td>Google TF serving containers for deployment</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Distributed Training</td><td>Scale across GPUs/TPUs</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Model Registry / Endpoints</td><td>Store TF models, serve online predictions</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0055","card":"q-gcp-ml-011-6-tensorflow-and-mnist-on-vertex-ai","sec":"gcp-ml-s012","q":"What is MNIST?","a":"<p>The \"Hello World\" of ML: 70,000 grayscale images of handwritten digits 0–9, 28×28 pixels, an image-classification benchmark.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0056","card":"q-gcp-ml-011-6-tensorflow-and-mnist-on-vertex-ai","sec":"gcp-ml-s012","q":"How do you load MNIST and normalize pixel values in TensorFlow?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import tensorflow as tf\nmnist = tf.keras.datasets.mnist\n(x_train, y_train), (x_test, y_test) = mnist.load_data()\n# Normalize pixel values (0-255 → 0-1)\nx_train, x_test = x_train / 255.0, x_test / 255.0</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0057","card":"q-gcp-ml-011-6-tensorflow-and-mnist-on-vertex-ai","sec":"gcp-ml-s012","q":"What is the beginner MNIST model in TensorFlow?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model = tf.keras.models.Sequential([\n    tf.keras.layers.Flatten(input_shape=(28, 28)),\n    tf.keras.layers.Dense(128, activation=&#x27;relu&#x27;),\n    tf.keras.layers.Dropout(0.2),\n    tf.keras.layers.Dense(10, activation=&#x27;softmax&#x27;)\n])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0058","card":"q-gcp-ml-011-6-tensorflow-and-mnist-on-vertex-ai","sec":"gcp-ml-s012","q":"How do you compile, train and evaluate the beginner MNIST model?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.compile(\n    optimizer=&#x27;adam&#x27;,\n    loss=&#x27;sparse_categorical_crossentropy&#x27;,\n    metrics=[&#x27;accuracy&#x27;]\n)\nmodel.fit(x_train, y_train, epochs=5)\nloss, accuracy = model.evaluate(x_test, y_test)\nprint(f&quot;Test accuracy: {accuracy:.4f}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0059","card":"q-gcp-ml-011-6-tensorflow-and-mnist-on-vertex-ai","sec":"gcp-ml-s012","q":"How do you predict on 5 MNIST test images and print the predicted and actual digit?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import numpy as np\npredictions = model.predict(x_test[:5])\nfor i, pred in enumerate(predictions):\n    print(f&quot;Image {i}: predicted={np.argmax(pred)}, actual={y_test[i]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0060","card":"q-gcp-ml-011-6-tensorflow-and-mnist-on-vertex-ai","sec":"gcp-ml-s012","q":"How do you save a TensorFlow model for deployment to Vertex AI?","a":"<p>Save it with <code>model.save</code>, then upload it to GCS.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.save(&quot;mnist_model&quot;)\nprint(&quot;Model saved to ./mnist_model&quot;)\n# Upload to GCS for Vertex AI\n# !gsutil cp -r mnist_model gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/models/mnist_model</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0061","card":"q-gcp-ml-011-6-tensorflow-and-mnist-on-vertex-ai","sec":"gcp-ml-s012","q":"What should you do with the tensorflow.org MNIST tutorials before building custom models on Vertex AI?","a":"<p>Work through both the beginner and expert versions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0062","card":"q-gcp-ml-012-comparison","sec":"gcp-ml-s013","q":"Colab Enterprise vs Managed Notebooks vs User-Managed Notebooks vs Instances in Vertex AI?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Control</th><th>Environment</th><th>VM/SSH</th><th>Patching</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Colab Enterprise</strong></td><td>Low</td><td>Pre-configured</td><td>No</td><td>Google</td><td>Trying open-source libraries, migrating from public Colab</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Managed Notebooks</strong></td><td>Medium (PaaS)</td><td>Pre-built Python containers</td><td>No</td><td>Google, auto-versioned</td><td>Resource monitoring, GPU testing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>User-Managed Notebooks</strong></td><td>High (IaaS)</td><td>TensorFlow, PyTorch, custom</td><td>Yes (SSH)</td><td>You</td><td>Full OS control, custom libraries</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Instances (new, recommended)</strong></td><td>High</td><td>JupyterLab 3, GPU-ready frameworks</td><td>Yes</td><td>Google</td><td>Production notebook work</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0063","card":"q-gcp-ml-012-comparison","sec":"gcp-ml-s013","q":"What can you do in Colab Enterprise?","a":"<p>Upload notebooks from local or public Colab, and configure resources with <strong>runtime templates</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0064","card":"q-gcp-ml-012-comparison","sec":"gcp-ml-s013","q":"What do User-managed notebooks (legacy DLVMs) offer?","a":"<p>JupyterLab 3 plus GPU frameworks, customizable OS/networking, and SSH to the VM. Full control means full responsibility.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0065","card":"q-gcp-ml-012-comparison","sec":"gcp-ml-s013","q":"What do Managed notebooks offer?","a":"<p>No VM access, built-in CPU/memory/GPU meters, <strong>executions and schedules</strong> for recurring runs, and an optional custom container via gcloud.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0066","card":"q-gcp-ml-012-comparison","sec":"gcp-ml-s013","q":"What are Vertex AI notebook Instances?","a":"<p>They combine managed and user-managed features. Google recommends them and encourages migration off managed and user-managed notebooks.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0067","card":"q-gcp-ml-012-comparison","sec":"gcp-ml-s013","q":"Which feature differences exist between User-Managed, Managed and Instances notebooks?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>User-Managed</th><th>Managed</th><th><strong>Instances</strong></th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>VM/SSH access</td><td>✅</td><td>❌</td><td>✅</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Dynamic GPU attach</td><td>❌ (recreate instance)</td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>UI resource meters</td><td>❌ (terminal only)</td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>JupyterLab 3</td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>GPU-enabled ML frameworks</td><td>✅</td><td>Limited</td><td>✅</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Google-managed patching</td><td>❌</td><td>✅</td><td>✅</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0068","card":"q-gcp-ml-013-comparison","sec":"gcp-ml-s013","q":"How do you create a user-managed notebook, SSH into it and get the JupyterLab URL?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud notebooks instances create mnist-user \\\n  --location=us-central1-a \\\n  --vm-image-project=deeplearning-platform-release \\\n  --vm-image-family=tf-latest-gpu \\\n  --machine-type=n1-standard-4\ngcloud compute ssh mnist-user --zone=us-central1-a\ngcloud notebooks instances describe mnist-user \\\n  --location=us-central1-a \\\n  --format=&quot;value(proxyUri)&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0069","card":"q-gcp-ml-013-comparison","sec":"gcp-ml-s013","q":"How do you create a managed notebook and list all notebook instances?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud notebooks instances create mnist-managed \\\n  --location=us-central1-a \\\n  --kernel=python3 \\\n  --machine-type=n1-standard-4\ngcloud notebooks instances list --location=us-central1-a --format=table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0070","card":"q-gcp-ml-013-comparison","sec":"gcp-ml-s013","q":"How do you schedule a notebook execution on a managed notebook?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud notebooks executions create \\\n  --display-name=&quot;mnist-daily-run&quot; \\\n  --location=us-central1-a \\\n  --notebook-instance=mnist-managed \\\n  --input-notebook-file=&quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/notebooks/mnist.ipynb&quot; \\\n  --output-notebook-folder=&quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/outputs/&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0071","card":"q-gcp-ml-013-comparison","sec":"gcp-ml-s013","q":"How do you create a new-type Workbench Instance, SSH into it and get the JupyterLab URL?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud workbench instances create mnist-instance \\\n  --location=us-central1-a \\\n  --machine-type=n1-standard-4\ngcloud compute ssh mnist-instance --zone=us-central1-a\ngcloud workbench instances describe mnist-instance \\\n  --location=us-central1-a \\\n  --format=&quot;value(proxyUri)&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0072","card":"q-gcp-ml-013-comparison","sec":"gcp-ml-s013","q":"How do you dynamically attach a GPU to a Workbench Instance?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud workbench instances update mnist-instance \\\n  --location=us-central1-a \\\n  --machine-type=n1-standard-8 \\\n  --accelerator-type=NVIDIA_TESLA_T4 \\\n  --accelerator-core-count=1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0073","card":"q-gcp-ml-013-comparison","sec":"gcp-ml-s013","q":"How do you list, stop and delete Workbench Instances?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud workbench instances list --location=us-central1-a --format=table\ngcloud workbench instances stop mnist-instance --location=us-central1-a\ngcloud workbench instances delete mnist-instance --location=us-central1-a</code></pre></div>\n<p>Stop saves cost.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0074","card":"q-gcp-ml-014-gpu-scaling-and-cost","sec":"gcp-ml-s014","q":"When does a notebook use the GPU in an ML workflow?","a":"<p>Only during <strong>training (epochs)</strong>, where linear algebra runs on the GPU. Data loading, model building, evaluation and prediction leave it idle.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0075","card":"q-gcp-ml-014-gpu-scaling-and-cost","sec":"gcp-ml-s014","q":"How do you size GPUs and control GPU cost in Vertex AI notebooks?","a":"<p>Use the real-time meters to size GPUs and detach them when not needed.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0076","card":"q-gcp-ml-014-gpu-scaling-and-cost","sec":"gcp-ml-s014","q":"How do you add a GPU to a managed notebook?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud notebooks instances update mnist-managed \\\n  --location=us-central1-a \\\n  --machine-type=n1-standard-8 \\\n  --accelerator-type=NVIDIA_TESLA_T4 \\\n  --accelerator-core-count=1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0077","card":"q-gcp-ml-014-gpu-scaling-and-cost","sec":"gcp-ml-s014","q":"How do you check the machine type and accelerator of a managed notebook?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud notebooks instances describe mnist-managed \\\n  --location=us-central1-a \\\n  --format=&quot;table(name, machineType, acceleratorConfig)&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0078","card":"q-gcp-ml-014-gpu-scaling-and-cost","sec":"gcp-ml-s014","q":"How do you verify that TensorFlow sees the GPU?","a":"<p>No code changes are needed to use the GPU. List the physical devices:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gpus = tf.config.list_physical_devices(&#x27;GPU&#x27;)\nprint(f&quot;GPUs available: {len(gpus)}&quot;)\nfor gpu in gpus:\n    print(f&quot;  {gpu.name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0079","card":"q-gcp-ml-015-challenge-set-up-a-notebook-for-the-expe","sec":"gcp-ml-s015","q":"Which notebook type is the best choice for the expert MNIST challenge and why?","a":"<p>An <strong>Instance</strong>: it has SSH like user-managed and dynamic sizing/GPU like managed.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0080","card":"q-gcp-ml-015-challenge-set-up-a-notebook-for-the-expe","sec":"gcp-ml-s015","q":"How do you get the expert MNIST notebook into a Vertex AI Instance?","a":"<p>Open the expert MNIST notebook from tensorflow.org in public Colab, download the <code>.ipynb</code>, and upload it into the instance.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0081","card":"q-gcp-ml-015-challenge-set-up-a-notebook-for-the-expe","sec":"gcp-ml-s015","q":"What settings do you pick for the expert MNIST Instance?","a":"<p>A machine type with a GPU, the TensorFlow runtime, and then watch the resource meter.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0082","card":"q-gcp-ml-015-challenge-set-up-a-notebook-for-the-expe","sec":"gcp-ml-s015","q":"How much GPU did expert MNIST training use, and what does that mean?","a":"<p>Training (5 epochs) used about <strong>50% of one GPU</strong>, so one GPU is enough. More would waste money.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0083","card":"q-gcp-ml-015-challenge-set-up-a-notebook-for-the-expe","sec":"gcp-ml-s015","q":"What caveat applies to GPU types when setting up a notebook?","a":"<p>At recording, 5 GPU types were available and not all are compatible with every base image. Test before scaling.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0084","card":"q-gcp-ml-015-challenge-set-up-a-notebook-for-the-expe","sec":"gcp-ml-s015","q":"Which command creates an Instance with a GPU for the expert MNIST challenge?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud workbench instances create mnist-expert \\\n  --location=us-central1-a \\\n  --machine-type=n1-standard-4 \\\n  --accelerator-type=NVIDIA_TESLA_T4 \\\n  --accelerator-core-count=1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0085","card":"q-gcp-ml-015-challenge-set-up-a-notebook-for-the-expe","sec":"gcp-ml-s015","q":"How do you list GPU types for a zone and stop the instance when done?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud compute accelerator-types list --filter=&quot;zone:us-central1-a&quot; --format=table\ngcloud workbench instances stop mnist-expert --location=us-central1-a</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0086","card":"q-gcp-ml-015-challenge-set-up-a-notebook-for-the-expe","sec":"gcp-ml-s015","q":"How does the expert MNIST CNN reshape the data and define its layers?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>x_train = x_train.reshape(-1, 28, 28, 1).astype(&#x27;float32&#x27;) / 255.0\nx_test = x_test.reshape(-1, 28, 28, 1).astype(&#x27;float32&#x27;) / 255.0\nmodel = tf.keras.models.Sequential([\n    tf.keras.layers.Conv2D(32, (3, 3), activation=&#x27;relu&#x27;, input_shape=(28, 28, 1)),\n    tf.keras.layers.MaxPooling2D((2, 2)),\n    tf.keras.layers.Conv2D(64, (3, 3), activation=&#x27;relu&#x27;),\n    tf.keras.layers.MaxPooling2D((2, 2)),\n    tf.keras.layers.Flatten(),\n    tf.keras.layers.Dense(64, activation=&#x27;relu&#x27;),\n    tf.keras.layers.Dropout(0.2),\n    tf.keras.layers.Dense(10, activation=&#x27;softmax&#x27;)\n])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0087","card":"q-gcp-ml-015-challenge-set-up-a-notebook-for-the-expe","sec":"gcp-ml-s015","q":"How does the expert MNIST model train?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.fit(x_train, y_train, epochs=5, batch_size=64, validation_split=0.1)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0088","card":"q-gcp-ml-016-8-vector-search-embeddings-ann-rag","sec":"gcp-ml-s016","q":"What is vector search?","a":"<p>Retrieval by <strong>semantic similarity</strong> instead of keywords.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0089","card":"q-gcp-ml-016-8-vector-search-embeddings-ann-rag","sec":"gcp-ml-s016","q":"What are embeddings, similarity metrics and ANN in vector search?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Concept</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Embeddings</strong></td><td>Text/images/audio turned into low-dimensional numeric vectors that capture meaning (like fingerprints)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Similarity metrics</strong></td><td>Distance between vectors; closer means more similar</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Approximate Nearest Neighbor (ANN)</strong></td><td>Algorithm that finds a query vector's nearest neighbors quickly</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0090","card":"q-gcp-ml-016-8-vector-search-embeddings-ann-rag","sec":"gcp-ml-s016","q":"Why is vector search critical for RAG?","a":"<p>Embeddings plus vector search ground LLM responses in real data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0091","card":"q-gcp-ml-016-8-vector-search-embeddings-ann-rag","sec":"gcp-ml-s016","q":"Vertex AI Vector Search vs open-source options like ChromaDB and Pinecone?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Vertex AI Vector Search</th><th>Open-source (ChromaDB, Pinecone)</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Hosting</td><td>Managed in Vertex AI</td><td>Self-hosted or SaaS</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Integration</td><td>Native (BigQuery, GCS, Vertex AI)</td><td>Standalone</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>GCP-native ML workflows</td><td>Multi-cloud or local development</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0092","card":"q-gcp-ml-016-8-vector-search-embeddings-ann-rag","sec":"gcp-ml-s016","q":"How do you list existing vector search indexes with the Vertex AI SDK?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>indexes = aiplatform.MatchingEngineIndex.list()\nfor idx in indexes:\n    print(f&quot;{idx.display_name} — {idx.resource_name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0093","card":"q-gcp-ml-017-stack-overflow-example-workflow","sec":"gcp-ml-s017","q":"What are the steps of the Vertex AI Vector Search Stack Overflow example?","a":"<ol>\n  <li>Load Stack Overflow Q&amp;A from the BigQuery public dataset.</li>\n  <li>Generate embeddings with the Vertex AI Text Embeddings API.</li>\n  <li>Upload embeddings to a GCS bucket.</li>\n  <li>Create an ANN index.</li>\n  <li>Create an index endpoint.</li>\n  <li>Deploy the index to the endpoint.</li>\n  <li>Query: encode the query text, find nearest neighbors.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0094","card":"q-gcp-ml-017-stack-overflow-example-workflow","sec":"gcp-ml-s017","q":"How does the Stack Overflow example read data from BigQuery for embeddings?","a":"<p>It queries the public dataset in chunks, because the data is too large for memory, and combines title and body for richer embeddings.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SELECT id, title, body, tags\nFROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`\nWHERE tags LIKE &#x27;%tensorflow%&#x27;\nLIMIT 10000</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0095","card":"q-gcp-ml-017-stack-overflow-example-workflow","sec":"gcp-ml-s017","q":"In the Vertex AI Vector Search Stack Overflow workflow, how do you read BigQuery results in chunks and combine title and body?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def query_bigquery_chunks(query, chunk_size=1000):\n    df = client.query(query).to_dataframe()\n    for i in range(0, len(df), chunk_size):\n        yield df[i:i + chunk_size]\n# Combine title and body for richer embeddings\nfor chunk in query_bigquery_chunks(query):\n    chunk[&#x27;title_with_body&#x27;] = chunk[&#x27;title&#x27;] + &#x27; &#x27; + chunk[&#x27;body&#x27;]\n    print(f&quot;Processed chunk: {len(chunk)} rows&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0096","card":"q-gcp-ml-017-stack-overflow-example-workflow","sec":"gcp-ml-s017","q":"How do you generate text embeddings with Vertex AI and how many dimensions do they have?","a":"<p>Use <code>TextEmbeddingModel</code> with <code>textembedding-gecko</code>. The embeddings have 768 dimensions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from vertexai.language_models import TextEmbeddingModel\nmodel = TextEmbeddingModel.from_pretrained(&quot;textembedding-gecko&quot;)\ntexts = [&quot;How to install GPU for TensorFlow&quot;, &quot;Python memory error fix&quot;]\nembeddings = model.get_embeddings(texts)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0097","card":"q-gcp-ml-017-stack-overflow-example-workflow","sec":"gcp-ml-s017","q":"How do you create a GCS bucket for embeddings and upload the embeddings file?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gsutil mb -l us-central1 gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;-embeddings\ngsutil cp embeddings.json gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;-embeddings/</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0098","card":"q-gcp-ml-017-stack-overflow-example-workflow","sec":"gcp-ml-s017","q":"How do you create a tree-AH ANN index in Vertex AI?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>index = aiplatform.MatchingEngineIndex.create_tree_ah_index(\n    display_name=&quot;stackoverflow-index&quot;,\n    contents_delta_uri=&quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;-embeddings/&quot;,\n    dimensions=768,\n    approximate_neighbors_count=10\n)\nprint(f&quot;Index created: {index.resource_name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0099","card":"q-gcp-ml-017-stack-overflow-example-workflow","sec":"gcp-ml-s017","q":"How do you create the index endpoint for Vertex AI Vector Search?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>index_endpoint = aiplatform.MatchingEngineIndexEndpoint.create(\n    display_name=&quot;stackoverflow-endpoint&quot;,\n    public_endpoint_enabled=True\n)\nprint(f&quot;Endpoint created: {index_endpoint.resource_name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0100","card":"q-gcp-ml-017-stack-overflow-example-workflow","sec":"gcp-ml-s017","q":"How do you deploy an index to an index endpoint?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>index_endpoint.deploy_index(\n    index=index,\n    deployed_index_id=&quot;stackoverflow_deployed&quot;,\n    display_name=&quot;stackoverflow-deployed-index&quot;\n)\nprint(&quot;Index deployed successfully&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0101","card":"q-gcp-ml-017-stack-overflow-example-workflow","sec":"gcp-ml-s017","q":"How do you query a deployed index for nearest neighbors?","a":"<p>Encode the text, then call <code>find_neighbors</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query_text = &quot;installed GPU for TensorFlow&quot;\nquery_embedding = model.get_embeddings([query_text])[0].values\nresponse = index_endpoint.find_neighbors(\n    deployed_index_id=&quot;stackoverflow_deployed&quot;,\n    queries=[query_embedding],\n    num_neighbors=5\n)\nfor neighbor in response[0]:\n    print(f&quot;ID: {neighbor.id}, Distance: {neighbor.distance:.4f}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0102","card":"q-gcp-ml-017-stack-overflow-example-workflow","sec":"gcp-ml-s017","q":"How do you verify that the deployed vector count matches the embeddings count?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>deployed_indexes = index_endpoint.deployed_indexes\nfor di in deployed_indexes:\n    print(f&quot;Deployed index: {di.id}&quot;)\n    print(f&quot;Vector count: {index.index_stats.vectors_count}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0103","card":"q-gcp-ml-017-stack-overflow-example-workflow","sec":"gcp-ml-s017","q":"How do you inspect indexes in the console and read index endpoint logs?","a":"<p>Console: Vertex AI, Vector Search, Indexes (vector count, algorithm, dimensions, endpoints).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud logging read &quot;resource.type=aiplatform.googleapis.com/IndexEndpoint&quot; --limit=10</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0104","card":"q-gcp-ml-017-stack-overflow-example-workflow","sec":"gcp-ml-s017","q":"How long can the Stack Overflow vector search notebook take and which steps are slowest?","a":"<p>It can take <strong>1.5+ hours</strong>. Embedding generation and index creation are the slowest steps.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0105","card":"q-gcp-ml-018-9-feature-store","sec":"gcp-ml-s018","q":"What is Vertex AI Feature Store?","a":"<p>A cloud-native feature management service, tightly integrated with <strong>BigQuery</strong>. It acts as a <strong>metadata layer on top of BigQuery</strong>, enabling online serving without duplicating data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0106","card":"q-gcp-ml-018-9-feature-store","sec":"gcp-ml-s018","q":"What are the benefits of Vertex AI Feature Store?","a":"<p>Centralized feature discovery/access/governance, <strong>online</strong> (real-time) and <strong>offline</strong> (historical/batch) serving, and native integration with training and prediction.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0107","card":"q-gcp-ml-018-9-feature-store","sec":"gcp-ml-s018","q":"Feature Store vs a database vs a GCS bucket for features?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Feature Store</th><th>Database</th><th>GCS Bucket</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Centralized, governed management</td><td>✅</td><td>❌ manual</td><td>❌ manual</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Online serving</td><td>✅ low latency</td><td>✅ possible</td><td>❌ not designed for it</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Offline serving</td><td>✅ via BigQuery</td><td>✅ possible</td><td>✅ batch reads</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Feature versioning</td><td>✅ built-in</td><td>❌ manual</td><td>❌ manual</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Metadata</td><td>✅ rich</td><td>limited</td><td>❌ none</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0108","card":"q-gcp-ml-018-9-feature-store","sec":"gcp-ml-s018","q":"What are the steps to use Vertex AI Feature Store?","a":"<p>Prepare feature data (BigQuery table/view), create the Feature Store (specify BigQuery source), define features (names, types, metadata), then serve online or offline.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0109","card":"q-gcp-ml-018-9-feature-store","sec":"gcp-ml-s018","q":"How do you list existing Feature Stores with the SDK?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>featurestores = aiplatform.Featurestore.list()\nfor fs in featurestores:\n    print(f&quot;{fs.display_name} — {fs.resource_name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0110","card":"q-gcp-ml-019-challenge-solution-feature-store-with-th","sec":"gcp-ml-s019","q":"Which notebook type does the Penguins Feature Store challenge run in?","a":"<p>An Instance-type notebook.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0111","card":"q-gcp-ml-019-challenge-solution-feature-store-with-th","sec":"gcp-ml-s019","q":"How do you load the public Penguins dataset and build an <code>entity_id</code> column?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query = &quot;&quot;&quot;\nSELECT *\nFROM `bigquery-public-data.ml_datasets.penguins`\nWHERE body_mass_g IS NOT NULL\n&quot;&quot;&quot;\ndf = bq_client.query(query).to_dataframe()\ndf = df.dropna()\n# Format: entity_id, feature columns\ndf[&#x27;entity_id&#x27;] = df.index.astype(str)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0112","card":"q-gcp-ml-019-challenge-solution-feature-store-with-th","sec":"gcp-ml-s019","q":"How do you create a Feature Store with one online node, and how long does it take?","a":"<p>It takes about 15 minutes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>featurestore = aiplatform.Featurestore.create(\n    featurestore_id=&quot;penguins_featurestore&quot;,\n    online_store_fixed_node_count=1\n)\nprint(f&quot;Feature Store created: {featurestore.resource_name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0113","card":"q-gcp-ml-019-challenge-solution-feature-store-with-th","sec":"gcp-ml-s019","q":"What is an entity type in Feature Store and how do you create one?","a":"<p>An entity type groups semantically related features.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>entity_type = featurestore.create_entity_type(\n    entity_type_id=&quot;penguins&quot;,\n    description=&quot;Penguin measurements&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0114","card":"q-gcp-ml-019-challenge-solution-feature-store-with-th","sec":"gcp-ml-s019","q":"How do you define the Penguins features and create them in batch?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>features = [\n    {&quot;feature_id&quot;: &quot;species&quot;, &quot;value_type&quot;: &quot;STRING&quot;},\n    {&quot;feature_id&quot;: &quot;island&quot;, &quot;value_type&quot;: &quot;STRING&quot;},\n    {&quot;feature_id&quot;: &quot;culmen_length_mm&quot;, &quot;value_type&quot;: &quot;DOUBLE&quot;},\n    {&quot;feature_id&quot;: &quot;culmen_depth_mm&quot;, &quot;value_type&quot;: &quot;DOUBLE&quot;},\n    {&quot;feature_id&quot;: &quot;flipper_length_mm&quot;, &quot;value_type&quot;: &quot;DOUBLE&quot;},\n    {&quot;feature_id&quot;: &quot;body_mass_g&quot;, &quot;value_type&quot;: &quot;DOUBLE&quot;},\n    {&quot;feature_id&quot;: &quot;sex&quot;, &quot;value_type&quot;: &quot;STRING&quot;},\n]\nentity_type.batch_create_features(feature_configs={\n    f[&quot;feature_id&quot;]: {&quot;value_type&quot;: f[&quot;value_type&quot;]} for f in features\n})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0115","card":"q-gcp-ml-019-challenge-solution-feature-store-with-th","sec":"gcp-ml-s019","q":"How do you write features from a DataFrame into a Feature Store?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>entity_type.ingest_from_df(\n    feature_ids=[f[&quot;feature_id&quot;] for f in features],\n    feature_time=&quot;feature_timestamp&quot;,\n    df_source=df,\n    entity_id_field=&quot;entity_id&quot;\n)\nprint(&quot;Features ingested successfully&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0116","card":"q-gcp-ml-019-challenge-solution-feature-store-with-th","sec":"gcp-ml-s019","q":"How do you read features back from a Feature Store?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>entity_ids = [&quot;0&quot;, &quot;1&quot;, &quot;2&quot;]\nresult = entity_type.read(entity_ids=entity_ids)\nprint(result)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0117","card":"q-gcp-ml-019-challenge-solution-feature-store-with-th","sec":"gcp-ml-s019","q":"What can you do in the Feature Store console?","a":"<p>View feature info/properties/metrics, enable <strong>feature monitoring</strong> (drift), and configure <strong>streaming ingestion</strong> or batch serving.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0118","card":"q-gcp-ml-019-challenge-solution-feature-store-with-th","sec":"gcp-ml-s019","q":"Which gcloud commands list, describe and delete a Feature Store?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud ai featurestores list --region=us-central1 --format=table\ngcloud ai featurestores describe penguins_featurestore --region=us-central1\ngcloud ai featurestores delete penguins_featurestore --region=us-central1 --force</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0119","card":"q-gcp-ml-020-10-model-registry","sec":"gcp-ml-s020","q":"What is the Vertex AI Model Registry?","a":"<p>A <strong>central repository</strong> for the model lifecycle in Vertex AI.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0120","card":"q-gcp-ml-020-10-model-registry","sec":"gcp-ml-s020","q":"What are the capabilities of Vertex AI Model Registry?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Organize models</td><td>One place for custom, AutoML, BigQuery ML models</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Version management</td><td>Multiple versions, default version, aliases and labels</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Deployment</td><td>Deploy registered models to Endpoints</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Lineage</td><td>Model details, artifacts, container images</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0121","card":"q-gcp-ml-020-10-model-registry","sec":"gcp-ml-s020","q":"Which model types does Vertex AI Model Registry support?","a":"<p><strong>Custom</strong> (TensorFlow, PyTorch…), <strong>AutoML</strong> (text, tabular, image, video), and <strong>BigQuery ML</strong> (trained with SQL).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0122","card":"q-gcp-ml-020-10-model-registry","sec":"gcp-ml-s020","q":"What is the Model Registry workflow?","a":"<p>Import/create model, assign version, add aliases/labels, deploy to Endpoint, predict.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0123","card":"q-gcp-ml-020-10-model-registry","sec":"gcp-ml-s020","q":"How do you list registered models and their versions with the SDK?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from google.cloud import aiplatform as aip\naip.init(project=&quot;&lt;your-project-id&gt;&quot;, location=&quot;us-central1&quot;)\nmodels = aip.Model.list()\nfor model in models:\n    print(f&quot;{model.display_name} — v{model.version_id} — {model.resource_name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0124","card":"q-gcp-ml-021-register-two-versions-of-a-model","sec":"gcp-ml-s021","q":"How do you get two pre-trained MobileNet models from TensorFlow Hub for the versioning exercise?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import tensorflow as tf\nimport tensorflow_hub as hub\nmodel_v1 = tf.keras.Sequential([\n    hub.KerasLayer(&quot;https://tfhub.dev/google/imagenet/mobilenet_v2_100_224/classification/5&quot;)\n])\nmodel_v1.build([None, 224, 224, 3])\nmodel_v2 = tf.keras.Sequential([\n    hub.KerasLayer(&quot;https://tfhub.dev/google/imagenet/mobilenet_v2_130_224/classification/5&quot;)\n])\nmodel_v2.build([None, 224, 224, 3])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0125","card":"q-gcp-ml-021-register-two-versions-of-a-model","sec":"gcp-ml-s021","q":"How do you save two model versions and upload them to GCS?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model_v1.save(&quot;model_v1&quot;)\nmodel_v2.save(&quot;model_v2&quot;)\n# !gsutil cp -r model_v1 gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/models/model_v1\n# !gsutil cp -r model_v2 gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/models/model_v2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0126","card":"q-gcp-ml-021-register-two-versions-of-a-model","sec":"gcp-ml-s021","q":"How do you upload version 1 of a model as the default with aliases?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model = aip.Model.upload(\n    display_name=&quot;my-model&quot;,\n    artifact_uri=&quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/models/model_v1&quot;,\n    serving_container_image_uri=&quot;us-docker.pkg.dev/vertex-ai/prediction/tf2-cpu.2-12:latest&quot;,\n    is_default_version=True,\n    version_aliases=[&quot;v1&quot;, &quot;stable&quot;],\n    version_description=&quot;Initial version&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0127","card":"q-gcp-ml-021-register-two-versions-of-a-model","sec":"gcp-ml-s021","q":"How do you upload version 2 as a new version of the same registered model?","a":"<p>Pass <code>parent_model</code> with the first model's resource name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model_v2_resource = aip.Model.upload(\n    display_name=&quot;my-model&quot;,\n    parent_model=model.resource_name,\n    artifact_uri=&quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/models/model_v2&quot;,\n    serving_container_image_uri=&quot;us-docker.pkg.dev/vertex-ai/prediction/tf2-cpu.2-12:latest&quot;,\n    is_default_version=False,\n    version_aliases=[&quot;v2&quot;, &quot;experimental&quot;],\n    version_description=&quot;Updated architecture&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0128","card":"q-gcp-ml-021-register-two-versions-of-a-model","sec":"gcp-ml-s021","q":"How do you list the versions and aliases of a registered model?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>versions = aip.Model.list(filter=f&#x27;display_name=&quot;my-model&quot;&#x27;)\nfor v in versions:\n    print(f&quot;Version: {v.version_id}, Aliases: {v.version_aliases}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0129","card":"q-gcp-ml-021-register-two-versions-of-a-model","sec":"gcp-ml-s021","q":"How do you list all registered models and show whether they are deployed?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>all_models = aip.Model.list()\nfor m in all_models:\n    print(f&quot;{m.display_name} — deployed: {bool(m.deployed_models)}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0130","card":"q-gcp-ml-022-11-endpoints-online-vs-batch-prediction","sec":"gcp-ml-s022","q":"Online vs Batch prediction in Vertex AI?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint needed</th><th>Use case</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Online</strong></td><td>Synchronous requests</td><td>✅ deploy model to an Endpoint</td><td>Real-time apps (web, mobile)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Batch</strong></td><td>Asynchronous job</td><td>❌ requested directly from the model</td><td>One-off or scheduled bulk predictions</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0131","card":"q-gcp-ml-022-11-endpoints-online-vs-batch-prediction","sec":"gcp-ml-s022","q":"What is a Vertex AI Endpoint?","a":"<p>It wraps compute (containers/VMs) around a model, so you do not set up Kubernetes or Cloud Run yourself.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0132","card":"q-gcp-ml-022-11-endpoints-online-vs-batch-prediction","sec":"gcp-ml-s022","q":"What is the Vertex AI deployment flow?","a":"<p>Train, save artifacts, upload to Model Registry, manage versions, then either online (create Endpoint, deploy, predict) or batch (submit job from the model, results).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0133","card":"q-gcp-ml-022-11-endpoints-online-vs-batch-prediction","sec":"gcp-ml-s022","q":"How do you create an Endpoint and deploy a model with autoscaling replicas?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>endpoint = aip.Endpoint.create(display_name=&quot;my-endpoint&quot;)\nprint(f&quot;Endpoint created: {endpoint.resource_name}&quot;)\nmodel.deploy(\n    endpoint=endpoint,\n    deployed_model_display_name=&quot;my-model-deployed&quot;,\n    machine_type=&quot;n1-standard-4&quot;,\n    min_replica_count=1,\n    max_replica_count=3\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0134","card":"q-gcp-ml-022-11-endpoints-online-vs-batch-prediction","sec":"gcp-ml-s022","q":"How do you list the models deployed on an Endpoint?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for deployed in endpoint.list_models():\n    print(f&quot;Model: {deployed.display_name}, Machine: {deployed.machine_type}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0135","card":"q-gcp-ml-022-11-endpoints-online-vs-batch-prediction","sec":"gcp-ml-s022","q":"How do you make an online prediction from a Vertex AI Endpoint?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>test_input = np.random.rand(1, 224, 224, 3).tolist()\nprediction = endpoint.predict(instances=test_input)\nprint(f&quot;Prediction: {prediction.predictions[0][:5]}...&quot;)  # First 5 values</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0136","card":"q-gcp-ml-022-11-endpoints-online-vs-batch-prediction","sec":"gcp-ml-s022","q":"How do you run a batch prediction without an Endpoint?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>batch_job = model.batch_predict(\n    job_display_name=&quot;my-batch-prediction&quot;,\n    instances_format=&quot;jsonl&quot;,\n    gcs_source=&quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/input/test_data.jsonl&quot;,\n    gcs_destination_prefix=&quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/output/&quot;,\n    machine_type=&quot;n1-standard-4&quot;\n)\nbatch_job.wait()\nprint(f&quot;Batch prediction complete: {batch_job.output_info}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0137","card":"q-gcp-ml-022-11-endpoints-online-vs-batch-prediction","sec":"gcp-ml-s022","q":"How do you undeploy models and delete a Vertex AI Endpoint?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>endpoint.undeploy_all()\nprint(&quot;All models undeployed&quot;)\nendpoint.delete()\nprint(&quot;Endpoint deleted&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0138","card":"q-gcp-ml-022-11-endpoints-online-vs-batch-prediction","sec":"gcp-ml-s022","q":"How do you list endpoints and where can you see their metrics in the console?","a":"<p>Console: Online Prediction, Endpoints, select endpoint (predictions/sec, latency, logs).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud ai endpoints list --region=us-central1 --format=table</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0139","card":"q-gcp-ml-023-12-vertex-ai-pipelines-mlops","sec":"gcp-ml-s023","q":"What is Vertex AI Pipelines?","a":"<p>A service to <strong>automate, monitor and govern ML systems serverlessly</strong> (managed Kubernetes underneath).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0140","card":"q-gcp-ml-023-12-vertex-ai-pipelines-mlops","sec":"gcp-ml-s023","q":"What features does Vertex AI Pipelines have?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Serverless</td><td>No infrastructure to manage</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Frameworks</td><td>Kubeflow Pipelines (KFP) or TensorFlow Extended (TFX)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>DAG visualization</td><td>Directed Acyclic Graph of steps</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Template Gallery</td><td>Pre-built templates for common workflows</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Custom templates</td><td>Upload your own</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0141","card":"q-gcp-ml-023-12-vertex-ai-pipelines-mlops","sec":"gcp-ml-s023","q":"Which Vertex AI components do Pipelines tie together?","a":"<p>Feature Store (features for training), Training, Model Registry, Endpoints, and Evaluation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0142","card":"q-gcp-ml-023-12-vertex-ai-pipelines-mlops","sec":"gcp-ml-s023","q":"What is the Vertex AI Pipelines Template Gallery and how do you use it?","a":"<p>Vertex AI, Pipelines, Template Gallery. Filter by type (e.g., \"Pipelines and Vertex AI\" is the easiest to run), view the DAG with node inputs/outputs, create a run from the UI or download to customize. Example: <strong>LLM Text Generation Evaluation</strong> (summarization, Q&amp;A, text generation).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0143","card":"q-gcp-ml-023-12-vertex-ai-pipelines-mlops","sec":"gcp-ml-s023","q":"How do you install the KFP SDK and import what a Vertex AI pipeline needs?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># !pip install kfp google-cloud-pipeline-components\nfrom kfp import compiler\nfrom kfp.dsl import pipeline, component\nfrom google.cloud import aiplatform as aip\naip.init(project=&quot;&lt;your-project-id&gt;&quot;, location=&quot;us-central1&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0144","card":"q-gcp-ml-023-12-vertex-ai-pipelines-mlops","sec":"gcp-ml-s023","q":"How do you define a simple KFP pipeline with two components and compile it?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@component\ndef train_model(dataset_uri: str) -&gt; str:\n    import tensorflow as tf\n    # Training logic here\n    model_path = &quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/models/trained_model&quot;\n    return model_path\n@component\ndef evaluate_model(model_path: str) -&gt; float:\n    # Evaluation logic here\n    accuracy = 0.95\n    return accuracy\n@pipeline(name=&quot;my-training-pipeline&quot;)\ndef training_pipeline(dataset_uri: str):\n    train_task = train_model(dataset_uri=dataset_uri)\n    eval_task = evaluate_model(model_path=train_task.output)\n# Compile the pipeline\ncompiler.Compiler().compile(\n    pipeline_func=training_pipeline,\n    package_path=&quot;training_pipeline.json&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0145","card":"q-gcp-ml-023-12-vertex-ai-pipelines-mlops","sec":"gcp-ml-s023","q":"How do you submit a compiled pipeline job to Vertex AI?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>job = aip.PipelineJob(\n    display_name=&quot;my-training-run&quot;,\n    template_path=&quot;training_pipeline.json&quot;,\n    parameter_values={&quot;dataset_uri&quot;: &quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/data/&quot;},\n    pipeline_root=&quot;gs://&lt;your-bucket&gt;/pipeline_root/&quot;\n)\njob.run(sync=False)\nprint(f&quot;Pipeline job submitted: {job.resource_name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0146","card":"q-gcp-ml-023-12-vertex-ai-pipelines-mlops","sec":"gcp-ml-s023","q":"Which gcloud commands list and describe Vertex AI pipeline jobs?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud ai pipelines jobs list --region=us-central1 --format=table\ngcloud ai pipelines jobs describe &lt;job-id&gt; --region=us-central1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0147","card":"q-gcp-ml-024-challenge-solution-custom-training-pipel","sec":"gcp-ml-s024","q":"What does the custom training pipeline challenge use and where does it run?","a":"<p>It runs in an Instance notebook. The template is custom training with pre-built Google Cloud Pipeline components (KFP sits on top of GKE).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0148","card":"q-gcp-ml-024-challenge-solution-custom-training-pipel","sec":"gcp-ml-s024","q":"Which imports does the custom training pipeline use?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># !pip install kfp google-cloud-pipeline-components\nfrom kfp import compiler\nfrom kfp.dsl import pipeline\nfrom google_cloud_pipeline_components.v1.custom_job import CustomTrainingJobOp\nfrom google_cloud_pipeline_components.v1.endpoint import EndpointCreateOp, ModelDeployOp\nfrom google_cloud_pipeline_components.v1.model import ModelUploadOp\nfrom google.cloud import aiplatform as aip\nimport uuid</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0149","card":"q-gcp-ml-024-challenge-solution-custom-training-pipel","sec":"gcp-ml-s024","q":"How is the pipeline configured with a project, region, bucket and service account?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>PROJECT_ID = &quot;&lt;your-project-id&gt;&quot;\nREGION = &quot;us-central1&quot;\nBUCKET_URI = f&quot;gs://{PROJECT_ID}-pipeline-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]}&quot;\nSERVICE_ACCOUNT = &quot;&lt;your-service-account&gt;@{PROJECT_ID}.iam.gserviceaccount.com&quot;\naip.init(project=PROJECT_ID, location=REGION, staging_bucket=BUCKET_URI)\n# Create the bucket\n# !gsutil mb -l {REGION} {BUCKET_URI}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0150","card":"q-gcp-ml-024-challenge-solution-custom-training-pipel","sec":"gcp-ml-s024","q":"How does the custom training pipeline define its training step?","a":"<p>It uses the pre-built Google component <code>CustomTrainingJobOp</code>, which is optimized for GCP.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>training_op = CustomTrainingJobOp(\n    display_name=&quot;custom-train&quot;,\n    project=project,\n    location=location,\n    worker_pool_specs=[{\n        &quot;machine_spec&quot;: {&quot;machine_type&quot;: &quot;n1-standard-4&quot;},\n        &quot;replica_count&quot;: 1,\n        &quot;python_package_spec&quot;: {\n            &quot;executor_image_uri&quot;: &quot;us-docker.pkg.dev/vertex-ai/training/tf-cpu.2-12:latest&quot;,\n            &quot;package_uris&quot;: [f&quot;{staging_bucket}/trainer.tar.gz&quot;],\n            &quot;python_module&quot;: &quot;trainer.task&quot;\n        }\n    }]\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0151","card":"q-gcp-ml-025-challenge-solution-custom-training-pipel","sec":"gcp-ml-s024","q":"How does the pipeline upload the model to the registry, create an endpoint and deploy?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model_op = ModelUploadOp(\n    project=project,\n    display_name=&quot;pipeline-model&quot;,\n    artifact_uri=f&quot;{staging_bucket}/model/&quot;,\n    serving_container_image_uri=&quot;us-docker.pkg.dev/vertex-ai/prediction/tf2-cpu.2-12:latest&quot;\n)\nendpoint_op = EndpointCreateOp(project=project, display_name=&quot;pipeline-endpoint&quot;)\ndeploy_op = ModelDeployOp(\n    model=model_op.outputs[&quot;model&quot;],\n    endpoint=endpoint_op.outputs[&quot;endpoint&quot;],\n    deployed_model_display_name=&quot;pipeline-deployed&quot;,\n    machine_type=&quot;n1-standard-4&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0152","card":"q-gcp-ml-025-challenge-solution-custom-training-pipel","sec":"gcp-ml-s024","q":"How do you compile the custom training pipeline?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>compiler.Compiler().compile(\n    pipeline_func=custom_training_pipeline,\n    package_path=&quot;custom_pipeline.json&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0153","card":"q-gcp-ml-025-challenge-solution-custom-training-pipel","sec":"gcp-ml-s024","q":"How do you run the custom training pipeline, and what does <code>sync=True</code> do?","a":"<p>It takes about 49 minutes. <code>sync=True</code> waits for completion.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>job = aip.PipelineJob(\n    display_name=&quot;custom-training-run&quot;,\n    template_path=&quot;custom_pipeline.json&quot;,\n    parameter_values={\n        &quot;project&quot;: PROJECT_ID,\n        &quot;location&quot;: REGION,\n        &quot;staging_bucket&quot;: BUCKET_URI\n    },\n    pipeline_root=f&quot;{BUCKET_URI}/pipeline_root/&quot;\n)\njob.run(sync=True)  # sync=True waits for completion\nprint(f&quot;Pipeline status: {job.state}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0154","card":"q-gcp-ml-025-challenge-solution-custom-training-pipel","sec":"gcp-ml-s024","q":"How do you evaluate a finished pipeline run in the Vertex AI UI?","a":"<p>In Vertex AI, Pipelines, Runs:</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>DAG</td><td>Click the run; completed steps are green</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Duration per step</td><td>Click a node; use timings for sizing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Logs</td><td>Click a node</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Model</td><td>Model Registry: verify the uploaded model</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Endpoint</td><td>Online Prediction: verify the deployment</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0155","card":"q-gcp-ml-025-challenge-solution-custom-training-pipel","sec":"gcp-ml-s024","q":"Which gcloud commands describe a pipeline job and read its logs?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud ai pipelines jobs describe &lt;job-id&gt; --region=us-central1\ngcloud logging read &quot;resource.type=aiplatform.googleapis.com/PipelineJob&quot; --limit=20</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0156","card":"q-gcp-ml-025-challenge-solution-custom-training-pipel","sec":"gcp-ml-s024","q":"Which commands clean up a pipeline's endpoint?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gcloud ai endpoints undeploy-model &lt;endpoint-id&gt; --region=us-central1 --deployed-model-id=&lt;model-id&gt;\ngcloud ai endpoints delete &lt;endpoint-id&gt; --region=us-central1</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0157","card":"q-gcp-ml-025-challenge-solution-custom-training-pipel","sec":"gcp-ml-s024","q":"What is the recommended approach for building Vertex AI pipelines?","a":"<p>Start from pre-built Google pipeline components, plug in custom ones where needed, and source-control pipeline templates for reproducibility.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0158","card":"q-gcp-ml-026-13-learning-path-and-resources","sec":"gcp-ml-s025","q":"What is the suggested learning order for Vertex AI?","a":"<p>(1) Vertex AI Studio and Gemini prompting, (2) Notebook Instances with TensorFlow, (3) Vector Search for RAG, (4) Feature Store, (5) Model Registry, (6) Endpoints (online/batch), (7) Pipelines for MLOps.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"gcp-ml-f0159","card":"q-gcp-ml-026-13-learning-path-and-resources","sec":"gcp-ml-s025","q":"Which links does the course list for Vertex AI learning?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Vertex AI docs: https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs</li>\n  <li>Notebook examples: https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/docs/tutorials/jupyter-notebooks</li>\n  <li>TensorFlow tutorials: https://www.tensorflow.org/tutorials</li>\n  <li>Google AI Studio: https://aistudio.google.com</li>\n  <li>Google Developer Experts community: https://developers.google.com/community/experts</li>\n</ul>","hand":true}];
